05:54:59,654 --> 05:55:02,154
After the specimen's imaged, the files are sent to DPO.

3848
05:55:02,734 --> 05:55:06,534
This is where we start the virtual data process. Here's a large overview.

3849
05:55:08,314 --> 05:55:11,714
To summarize briefly, images are given to

3850
05:55:11,774 --> 05:55:15,574
DPO for delivery. They go through a series of quality control measures.

3851
05:55:16,054 --> 05:55:19,894
Accepted images enter our digital asset management system called

3852
05:55:19,934 --> 05:55:23,314
DAMS. From the DAMS, we automatically create and publish

3853
05:55:23,834 --> 05:55:27,786
skeletal records into EMu We also have a simultaneous workflow

3854
05:55:27,826 --> 05:55:31,326
going where specimen label data from the label images are

3855
05:55:31,406 --> 05:55:35,346
transcribed, so that data can later be appended to the catalog records

3856
05:55:35,426 --> 05:55:35,846
in EMu.

3857
05:55:38,326 --> 05:55:41,146
A major aspect of this project is quality control.

3858
05:55:41,826 --> 05:55:43,766
For this, we use a program called OSPRY.

3859
05:55:44,506 --> 05:55:48,026
OSPRY is an open source application that was developed in-house by

3860
05:55:48,066 --> 05:55:50,646
DPO. You can find the source code on GitHub.

3861
05:55:51,386 --> 05:55:55,046
Also, there is a public side to OSPRY, so you can see images

3862
05:55:55,606 --> 05:55:58,106
in real time before they are published to EMu.

3863
05:56:02,626 --> 05:56:05,786
Images are assessed to ensure that quality standards are met.

3864
05:56:06,106 --> 05:56:09,826
Anywhere from 10% to 40% of the images of a folder are randomly

3865
05:56:09,886 --> 05:56:10,886
selected for QC.

3866
05:56:11,746 --> 05:56:14,646
We standardize phrasing to document when errors occur.

3867
05:56:18,246 --> 05:56:21,286
Errors that can occur on an image can simply be

3868
05:56:22,166 --> 05:56:23,386
