4203
06:18:27,806 --> 06:18:28,326
workflow.

4204
06:18:29,966 --> 06:18:33,526
So when we think about herbarium digitization, we often think about it as

4205
06:18:33,566 --> 06:18:34,946
having two layers.

4206
06:18:35,906 --> 06:18:39,686
One layer is the image of the specimen, and the

4207
06:18:39,766 --> 06:18:42,666
second layer is the transcribed label data.

4208
06:18:43,466 --> 06:18:47,206
And collectively, these two layers give you information about the

4209
06:18:47,286 --> 06:18:50,146
specimen's morphology, taxonomy,

4210
06:18:51,266 --> 06:18:53,826
collection, location, date, and so forth.

4211
06:18:54,826 --> 06:18:58,766
But there's a whole variety of additional information that can be captured from the

4212
06:18:58,806 --> 06:19:02,546
physical specimen, mobilized online, and attached to

4213
06:19:02,606 --> 06:19:04,526
this digital record of the specimen.

4214
06:19:05,266 --> 06:19:08,786
And at the Missouri Botanical Garden, one of those types of

4215
06:19:08,866 --> 06:19:12,486
information that we're particularly interested in is spectral

4216
06:19:12,526 --> 06:19:13,186
reflectance.

4217
06:19:14,546 --> 06:19:18,446
So what exactly is spectral reflectance, and why do we care

4218
06:19:18,526 --> 06:19:18,866
about it?

4219
06:19:20,066 --> 06:19:23,746
Well, spectral reflectance, simply put, is light reflectance

4220
06:19:23,806 --> 06:19:25,306
data. And

4221
06:19:26,366 --> 06:19:30,286
a more technical definition is that spectral reflectance is the

4222
06:19:30,326 --> 06:19:34,206
percent of light reflected by a surface across different wavelengths in

4223
06:19:34,266 --> 06:19:35,626
the electromagnetic spectrum.

4224
06:19:36,846 --> 06:19:40,746
And it's important because it encodes information about

4225
06:19:40,806 --> 06:19:44,706
the physical and chemical properties of whatever material is being

4226
06:19:44,766 --> 06:19:48,726
measured. So when you're taking a spectral reflectance measurement from a

4227
06:19:48,826 --> 06:19:52,126
leaf, you're capturing information about the plant's

4228
06:19:52,186 --> 06:19:56,026
chemistry and phenotype that are hard to capture in

4229
06:19:56,346 --> 06:19:57,086
other methods.

4230
06:19:58,156 --> 06:20:01,836
And you can use spectral reflectance to infer the value of a

4231
06:20:01,896 --> 06:20:05,576
variety of functional traits, and this data can be

4232
06:20:05,716 --> 06:20:08,396
used to assist with species identification.

4233
06:20:11,016 --> 06:20:14,316
So in 2024, we were fortunate to receive

4234
06:20:14,376 --> 06:20:18,296
philanthropic support to digitize our entire collection

4235
06:20:18,356 --> 06:20:20,396
of around eight million specimens.

4236
06:20:21,336 --> 06:20:21,796
And

4237
06:20:22,836 --> 06:20:25,216
in addition to digitizing our

4238
06:20:27,136 --> 06:20:30,756
collection, taking images and transcriptions of all of the

4239
06:20:30,815 --> 06:20:34,476
specimens in our collection, the support also is allowing us to

4240
06:20:34,556 --> 06:20:38,156
integrate the capture of spectral reflectance as a

4241
06:20:38,216 --> 06:20:39,876
third layer of digitization.

4242
06:20:42,096 --> 06:20:46,076
And I'll note that our herbarium, prior to this

4243
06:20:46,116 --> 06:20:49,776
project, had around two million specimens already

4244
06:20:49,856 --> 06:20:53,616
imaged and around four million transcribed, so this is finishing

4245
06:20:53,696 --> 06:20:56,516
out our digitization for the imaging and transcriptions.

4246
06:20:57,336 --> 06:21:01,236
And the spectral reflectance isn't being captured for every specimen in

4247
06:21:01,276 --> 06:21:03,656
our collection, but only a subset of our collection.

4248
06:21:05,056 --> 06:21:08,076
One third component of this project that I won't get into

4249
06:21:08,556 --> 06:21:10,196
detail about in this talk,

4250
06:21:11,096 --> 06:21:14,136
but I'll give a shout-out to and would be happy to talk about if anyone is

4251
06:21:14,196 --> 06:21:18,036
interested, is this also allowed us to launch a curatorial mentorship

4252
06:21:18,096 --> 06:21:21,656
program where all of the 18 digitization

4253
06:21:21,736 --> 06:21:25,616
staff hired on through this project are paired with a curator at the

4254
06:21:25,656 --> 06:21:29,596
Missouri Botanical Garden, and they get to learn taxonomic expertise in

4255
06:21:29,676 --> 06:21:32,656
one or more families and can actively help curate our collection.

4256
06:21:33,576 --> 06:21:37,476
All right. So the workflow that we follow for this

4257
06:21:37,536 --> 06:21:41,336
project begins by taking high-resolution images of

4258
06:21:41,416 --> 06:21:44,876
specimens using in-house digitization

4259
06:21:45,696 --> 06:21:46,636
photo stations,

4260
06:21:48,296 --> 06:21:51,616
where when specimens are imaged, they also receive a

4261
06:21:51,676 --> 06:21:54,096
barcode to serve as a unique identifier.

4262
06:21:55,276 --> 06:21:58,856
And after imaging, we send our images off to our

4263
06:21:58,916 --> 06:22:02,056
external transcription partner, Max Communications,

4264
06:22:03,096 --> 06:22:06,616
where they transcribe our specimens, send us our data back,

4265
06:22:07,176 --> 06:22:10,956
and we provide in-house quality

4266
06:22:11,016 --> 06:22:14,736
assurance on those data before uploading them to our collection management

4267
06:22:14,776 --> 06:22:15,716
system, Tropicos.

4268
06:22:16,836 --> 06:22:20,276
But in parallel, after specimens are imaged and

4269
06:22:20,336 --> 06:22:23,576
barcoded, they're also sent to our spectral measurement team,

4270
06:22:24,096 --> 06:22:27,856
where they take spectral reflectance measurements of leaves of

4271
06:22:28,356 --> 06:22:29,416
some of our specimens.

4272
06:22:30,856 --> 06:22:34,616
And the general workflow that we follow for taking these spectral

4273
06:22:34,676 --> 06:22:37,496
reflectance measurements is one where we're taking

4274
06:22:38,416 --> 06:22:41,856
three measurements per leaf surface for every

4275
06:22:41,936 --> 06:22:45,916
specimen. So something that I'll call out here is that we are

4276
06:22:45,996 --> 06:22:49,716
not taking spectral reflectance images of

4277
06:22:49,776 --> 06:22:53,576
entire specimens. Rather, we're taking point measurements of

4278
06:22:53,656 --> 06:22:56,836
specific areas on the leaves of specimens.

4279
06:22:57,596 --> 06:23:01,096
So this is simply spectroscopy for

4280
06:23:01,136 --> 06:23:02,316
herbarium specimens.

4281
06:23:03,236 --> 06:23:03,556
And

4282
06:23:05,176 --> 06:23:08,556
this technique cannot be done for all specimens because

4283
06:23:08,616 --> 06:23:12,276
we always have to ensure that we are taking a

4284
06:23:12,316 --> 06:23:15,676
measurement of a leaf on top of a non-reflective black

4285
06:23:15,716 --> 06:23:18,996
background. So this has to be done

4286
06:23:19,816 --> 06:23:23,696
on leaves that can be lifted from the herbarium

4287
06:23:23,756 --> 06:23:27,496
paper or that are stored in a fragment packet of an herbarium

4288
06:23:27,576 --> 06:23:31,496
specimen. And we take these measurements with the leaf on top of a black

4289
06:23:31,556 --> 06:23:35,296
background to ensure that whatever surface the leaf is on

4290
06:23:35,356 --> 06:23:37,536
top of is not affecting our spectral measurement.

4291
06:23:38,796 --> 06:23:42,276
We also restrict this work to specimens that

4292
06:23:42,916 --> 06:23:46,596
don't have contamination, like leaves that are heavily

4293
06:23:46,656 --> 06:23:50,556
glued or have pathogens or other types of contamination that might

4294
06:23:50,596 --> 06:23:52,156
affect our reflectance values.

4295
06:23:54,716 --> 06:23:58,556
So after we take our actual reflectance measurements,

4296
06:23:58,956 --> 06:24:02,616
we also capture a whole variety of metadata

4297
06:24:02,716 --> 06:24:06,236
associated with each individual scan, which will be

4298
06:24:06,276 --> 06:24:10,216
important for downstream analyses to be able to understand

4299
06:24:10,236 --> 06:24:12,376
the context in which the scans were taken.

4300
06:24:13,536 --> 06:24:17,455
So metadata that we're capturing, there's a whole variety of fields, but

4301
06:24:17,515 --> 06:24:20,576
some of them include the surface of the leaf that was measured,

4302
06:24:21,896 --> 06:24:25,836
the developmental stage of the leaf, the perceived specimen

4303
06:24:25,876 --> 06:24:29,556
preservation, and if there did happen to be

4304
06:24:29,656 --> 06:24:33,596
glue, pathogens, or other types of contamination on the area of the

4305
06:24:33,636 --> 06:24:37,216
leaf that was measured, we record that so that we can note it for downstream

4306
06:24:37,256 --> 06:24:37,856
analysis.

4307
06:24:39,276 --> 06:24:41,356
And this spectral

4308
06:24:42,516 --> 06:24:46,216
measurement protocol and the associated metadata, we

4309
06:24:46,276 --> 06:24:50,036
collaboratively developed with a group of like-minded researchers who are

4310
06:24:50,136 --> 06:24:53,716
all interested in taking spectral reflectance measurements from herbarium

4311
06:24:53,756 --> 06:24:57,196
specimens, which we call iHerbSpec, or the

4312
06:24:57,256 --> 06:25:00,356
International Herbarium Spectral Digitization Working Group.

4313
06:25:01,296 --> 06:25:04,996
And we first convened a little more than two years ago

4314
06:25:05,536 --> 06:25:09,336
and have developed the first standardized protocol for taking

4315
06:25:09,416 --> 06:25:13,196
spectral reflectance measurements from herbarium specimens with

4316
06:25:13,636 --> 06:25:17,236
file naming conventions and standardized

4317
06:25:17,296 --> 06:25:21,136
metadata fields that all of us in this group are using

4318
06:25:21,196 --> 06:25:24,876
for our own collections to ensure that we can

4319
06:25:26,476 --> 06:25:30,256
have our data be interoperable across institutions and reusable

4320
06:25:30,316 --> 06:25:31,056
into the future.

4321
06:25:32,856 --> 06:25:36,336
So today, iHerbSpec consists of more than 30

4322
06:25:36,396 --> 06:25:39,596
institutions, and we aim to meet in person

4323
06:25:40,316 --> 06:25:42,236
annually at least once per year.

4324
06:25:43,116 --> 06:25:46,976
We held our second annual in-person meeting at the Missouri Botanical Garden

4325
06:25:47,016 --> 06:25:50,796
this past May, where we discussed a governance structure for our

4326
06:25:50,876 --> 06:25:54,656
group and reviewed how the protocol went in its

