4355
06:27:35,004 --> 06:27:38,884
So you'll note that taking these spectral reflectance measurements is much

4356
06:27:38,924 --> 06:27:42,424
more time intensive than taking a traditional specimen image.

4357
06:27:42,824 --> 06:27:46,464
There's specimen selection involved, and you're taking multiple measurements per

4358
06:27:46,524 --> 06:27:47,104
specimen.

4359
06:27:49,204 --> 06:27:51,164
And in addition to

4360
06:27:52,124 --> 06:27:55,844
only being able to do this with specimens that meet our scanning

4361
06:27:55,884 --> 06:27:59,704
criteria, we're also, for now, restricting

4362
06:27:59,864 --> 06:28:03,784
which specimens we take spectral reflectance data on to

4363
06:28:03,864 --> 06:28:07,004
those that are both of woody taxa

4364
06:28:07,543 --> 06:28:11,244
that Missouri Botanical Garden curators have taxonomic expertise

4365
06:28:11,344 --> 06:28:11,584
in.

4366
06:28:13,384 --> 06:28:13,644
So

4367
06:28:14,564 --> 06:28:18,344
after we have these data, of course, the interesting question is what can you do

4368
06:28:18,364 --> 06:28:18,824
