4369
06:28:20,084 --> 06:28:20,704
And one

4370
06:28:22,584 --> 06:28:26,264
area that we've been particularly interested in is

4371
06:28:26,344 --> 06:28:30,224
training clade-specific species identification models on

4372
06:28:30,284 --> 06:28:33,804
spectra to then deploy on specimens

4373
06:28:33,844 --> 06:28:35,884
without a species level identification.

4374
06:28:37,104 --> 06:28:41,004
And we found that when you restrict to specimens that

4375
06:28:41,024 --> 06:28:44,484
are expert identified, so only those ones where you can really trust the

4376
06:28:44,524 --> 06:28:45,244
determination,

4377
06:28:46,464 --> 06:28:49,784
you typically get accuracies in the

4378
06:28:50,044 --> 06:28:50,924
90%.

4379
06:28:52,284 --> 06:28:53,604
So here, for example,

4380
06:28:55,604 --> 06:28:59,424
this is a confusion matrix for a species identification model

4381
06:28:59,904 --> 06:29:03,724
trained on reflectance spectra in the genus Pleurotherium in the

4382
06:29:03,804 --> 06:29:04,744
family Lauraceae.

4383
06:29:06,104 --> 06:29:09,684
How you can interpret this plot is the true identification of

4384
06:29:09,744 --> 06:29:13,204
specimens is on the Y, the predicted identification is on the

4385
06:29:13,444 --> 06:29:17,384
X-axis, and then the numbers in each cell are the

4386
06:29:17,424 --> 06:29:21,104
percent of times the model predicted specimens

4387
06:29:21,264 --> 06:29:24,644
of the true identification as each of these predicted identities.

4388
06:29:24,704 --> 06:29:28,644
So if the model is performing correctly, you expect this nice diagonal

4389
06:29:28,704 --> 06:29:30,544
running from the bottom left through the upper right.

4390
06:29:31,184 --> 06:29:35,084
And you can see that for many of these, we have accuracies in the mid-90s

4391
06:29:35,164 --> 06:29:38,984
or up. And over on the right is an example

4392
06:29:39,084 --> 06:29:43,064
of one Pleurotherium specimen that is sterile, so it's

4393
06:29:43,184 --> 06:29:46,644
lacking reproductive material. We couldn't identify it to species

4394
06:29:47,044 --> 06:29:50,924
based on morphology, but the spectra are predicting it

4395
06:29:51,004 --> 06:29:53,824
as Pleurotherium insigne 100% of the time.

4396
06:29:54,664 --> 06:29:58,364
So this is a method you can potentially use for

4397
06:29:58,524 --> 06:30:02,124
specimens only with leaf data to assign a species level identification.

4398
06:30:04,324 --> 06:30:08,084
So if you take away anything from this talk, I think there are three main

4399
06:30:08,164 --> 06:30:08,844
